# Allowlist for `mypy.stubtest`, read by scripts/run-all-checks.sh and CI.
#
# The supported imports are "from host_galileo import ..." and
# "from host_galileo.oops import ...", so the stubs of those two packages describe the
# whole public API. host_galileo.oops imports the module below, which is implementation
# detail and deliberately carries no stub; stubtest reports it as "failed to find stubs",
# which this file accepts. Nothing else is accepted: a public name missing from the two
# stubs still fails the check.
host_galileo\.oops\.ssi
